        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Acridine dyes are cell permeable, basic molecules with an acridine chromophore. These compounds intercalate DNA. The image shown represents the core structure of the acridine family, with specific dyes containing varying substituents.</obo:IAO_0000115>
