        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Mechanism of enzymatic degradation common to Ambler Class A, C and D beta-lactamases.  A serine residue located in the active site is used to form an acyl-enzyme intermediate and subsequent hydrolysis renders the beta-lactam inactive.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
