        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">OXY beta-lactamases are chromosomal class A beta-lactamases that are found in Klebsiella oxytoca. At constitutive low levels, OXY beta-lactamases confer resistance to aminopenicillins and carboxypenicillins. At high induced levels,  OXY beta-lactamases confer resistance to penicillins, cephalosporins and aztreonam.</owl:annotatedTarget>
