        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Daptomycin binds to the cytoplasmic membrane of Gram-positive. It&apos;s lipopeptide tail servers as a ion channel for potassium. This causes a rapid depolarization that result in failures in DNA/RNA/Protein synthesis. Eventually cell death.</owl:annotatedTarget>
