        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Klebsiella pneumoniae outer membrane porin protein. In beta-lactam-resistant Klebsiella, this porin is often deleted, limiting diffusion of the antibiotic into the cell. Klebsiella strains expressing OmpK35 are often beta-lactam sensitive even in the presence of beta-lactamases because of an inefficient mechanism.</obo:IAO_0000115>
