        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Edeine acetyltransferase enzymes catalyze the transfer of an acetyl group to active edeine, converting it to an inactive form in vivo. This mechanism is used for high-level self-resistance in edeine-producing Brevibacillus spp.</owl:annotatedTarget>
