        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Point mutations in the thymidylate synthetase thyA gene shown clinically to confer resistance to para-aminosalicylic acid. Loss-of-function mutations in thyA disrupt the catalytic activity and substrate-binding affinity, thus conferring resistance.</owl:annotatedTarget>
