        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Fosfomycin is transported bacterial cells through transporters, one of them being glycerol-3-phosphate, which is encoded by the GlpT gene. Mutations in the GlpT gene can confer resistance to fosfomycin.</obo:IAO_0000115>
