        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Enables the active transport of a solute across a membrane by a mechanism whereby two or more species are transported in opposite directions in a tightly coupled process not directly linked to a form of energy other than chemiosmotic energy. The reaction is: solute A(out) + solute B(in) = solute A(in) + solute B(out).</obo:IAO_0000115>
